# Todo Full-Stack Web Application - Environment Variables

## Shared Secret (CRITICAL)
Generate a secure secret for JWT signing and use the SAME value in both backend and frontend:

```bash
# Linux/Mac
openssl rand -hex 32

# Windows (PowerShell)
[Convert]::ToBase64String((1..32 | ForEach-Object { Get-Random -Maximum 256 }))
```

## Backend (.env)
Copy `backend/.env.example` to `backend/.env` and fill in:
- DATABASE_URL: Your Neon PostgreSQL connection string (use postgresql+asyncpg://)
- BETTER_AUTH_SECRET: The shared secret generated above
- FRONTEND_URL: Frontend URL for CORS (http://localhost:3000 for dev)

## Frontend (.env.local)
Copy `frontend/.env.local.example` to `frontend/.env.local` and fill in:
- NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: Backend API URL (http://localhost:8000 for dev)
- BETTER_AUTH_SECRET: The SAME shared secret as backend
- NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: Frontend URL (http://localhost:3000 for dev)

## Security Notes
- Never commit .env or .env.local files to version control
- Use different secrets for development and production
- Keep DATABASE_URL secure and never expose publicly
